-- title:
--   Drinfeld chart at a supersingular point: constants, equivariance, branch
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $q\ge 5$, a nonzero $M'$ with $q\nmid M'$, a prime $\ell\ge 3$ with $\ell\ne q$ and $\ell\nmid M'$, a field $L$ of characteristic zero that is a cyclotomic extension of $\mathbb{Q}$ of order $q\ell$, a primitive $q$-th root of unity $\zeta\in L$ and a primitive $(q\ell)$-th root of unity $\xi\in L$. Let $K$ be the intermediate field of $L\subset \mathrm{LaurentSeries}\,L$ generated over $L$ by the coefficientwise image of the $q$-expansion function field of $X_H$ of level $N_0=(q\ell)^2M'$, where $H=\mathrm{levelH}\,(q\ell)\,M'$ is the kernel of the reduction $(\mathbb{Z}/N_0)^\times\to(\mathbb{Z}/q\ell)^\times$. Let $A$ be a discrete valuation ring with fraction field $L$, with $q$ in its maximal ideal, with $\zeta$ in the image of $A$, with uniformiser $\varpi$ generating $\mathfrak m_A$, and with an $A$-algebra structure on $K$ compatible with $A\to L\to K$. Let $j\in K$ be nonzero with Laurent series the coefficientwise image of [`ModularCurve.jq`](def/ModularCurve_X0.html#L157). Let $X=\mathrm{TwoChartIntegralModel}\,A\,K\,j$, the pushout of the two maps $\mathrm{Spec}$ of the mid chart into $\mathrm{Spec}$ of the algebras of elements of $K$ integral over $A[j]$, respectively over $A[j^{-1}]$. Let $z\in X$ be a point at which the germ $\varpi z$ of the image of $\varpi$ under the structure morphism $X\to\mathrm{Spec}\,A$ lies in the maximal ideal of the stalk, let $y\in\mathrm{Spec}$ of the $j$-finite chart algebra satisfy $\iota_{\mathrm{Fin}}(y)=z$, and assume $y$ is supersingular: for every algebraically closed field $\Omega$ of characteristic $q$ and every ring homomorphism $\varphi$ from the $j$-finite chart algebra to $\Omega$ with kernel $y$, the value $\varphi(j)$ lies in $\mathrm{ssJSet}\,q\,\Omega$, i.e. every elliptic Weierstrass curve over $\Omega$ with that $j$-invariant has no nonzero point killed by $q$. Then there exist a complete discrete valuation ring $W$, a ring homomorphism $\sigma:A\to W$ with $\mathfrak m_W=(\sigma\varpi)$, power series $f,u,v\in W[[X_0,X_1]]$ with $u,v$ units and $f\equiv X_0X_1^q-X_0^qX_1 \pmod{(X_0,X_1)^{q+2}}$, and a ring isomorphism $e$ from the $\mathfrak m$-adic completion of the stalk $\mathcal O_{X,z}$ onto $S=W[[X_0,X_1]]/(\sigma\varpi\cdot v-f\cdot u)$, with the following three properties. First, $e$ carries the image in the completion of the germ of any $a\in A$ to the class of the constant $\sigma a$. Second, for every $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$ and every $L$-algebra automorphism $\tau$ of $K$ satisfying $\mathrm{IsLevelAutAt}\,L\,(q\ell)\,\xi\,(q\ell)\,N_0\,H\,\gamma^{-1}\,K\,\tau$ (for all weights $k$, all $\Gamma_H(N_0)$-forms $f_1,g$ of weight $k$ with integral $q$-expansions and $g\neq 0$, all $x\in K$ whose Laurent series is the coefficientwise image of the ratio of those $q$-expansions, and all embeddings $\iota:L\to\mathbb{C}$ with $\iota\xi=e^{2\pi i/(q\ell)}$, the image of $\tau x$ under $\iota$ times the $q$-expansion of $g\mid_k \mathrm{conjElemN}\,(q\ell)\,\gamma^{-1}$ equals that of $f_1\mid_k \mathrm{conjElemN}\,(q\ell)\,\gamma^{-1}$), such that $\tau$ preserves the $j$-finite chart algebra and induces the identity modulo $y$, there are a ring automorphism $\theta$ of $S$, an element $c\in W$ and a matrix $M\in M_2(W)$ with: $\theta$ intertwining, through $e$ and the germ map, with the restriction of $\tau$ to the chart algebra; $\theta$ fixing the classes of all constants from $W$; $\theta(X_{jj})\equiv\sum_{ii}M_{ii,jj}X_{ii}$ modulo the square of the ideal generated by the classes of $X_0,X_1$; $c^{q+1}\equiv 1$ and $M_{ii,jj}\equiv c\,\gamma_{ii,jj}$ modulo $\mathfrak m_W$; $c\equiv 1$ whenever $\gamma\in\Gamma(\ell)$; and $c\not\equiv 1$ whenever $\gamma\in\Gamma(q)$ and $\tau$ is not the identity. Third, for every prime ideal $P$ of $S$ not containing both classes of $X_0$ and $X_1$, containing the class of $\sigma\varpi$, and containing the class of $X_0+h$ for some $h\in(X_0,X_1)^2$, and for every $a$ in the $j$-finite chart algebra, the image of the germ of $a$ in the completion lies in $e^{-1}(P)$ if and only if every Laurent coefficient of $a$ lies in the image of $\mathfrak m_A$ in $L$.
--
--   This is the local description, at a supersingular point of the two-chart integral model over a discrete valuation ring above $q$, of the completed local ring as a Drinfeld-type chart $W[[X_0,X_1]]/(\varpi v-fu)$ with $f$ congruent to $X_0X_1^q-X_0^qX_1$, together with compatibility with the constants, the action of level automorphisms on linear parts, and the identification of the branch tangent to $X_0=0$ with the Gauss valuation on $q$-expansions. It is the existential core from which the packaged chart statements with further riders are assembled, and is used by two such downstream statements.
